+# Ramsey multiplicity constant of $K\_6$
+
+## Description of constant
+
+For a 2-colouring of the edges of $K\_n$, let $k\_6$ be the number of $6$-element vertex sets whose fifteen edges all have the same colour. The **Ramsey multiplicity constant of $K\_6$** is
+
+$$
+C_{89c} := \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{\min k_6}{\binom{n}{6}},
+$$
+
+the minimum over all 2-colourings of $K\_n$, or equivalently the minimum density of monochromatic $K\_6$ in a 2-edge-coloured graphon. It is often written $c\_6$. Erdős conjectured $C\_{89c} = 2^{1-15} = 2^{-14}$ [Erd1962]; Thomason disproved this for all $K\_t$ with $t \ge 4$ [Tho1989]. Bounds are usually quoted as multiples of $2^{-14}$. See [C89a](89a.html) and [C89b](89b.html) for $K\_4$ and $K\_5$.
+
+## Known upper bounds
+
+| Bound | Reference | Comments |
+| ----- | --------- | -------- |
+| $2^{-14} \approx 6.1035 \times 10^{-5}$ | [Erd1962] | Uniformly random colouring. Erdős conjectured that this is sharp. |
+| $0.936 \cdot 2^{-14}$ | [Tho1989] | As quoted in [Fra2002]. |
+| $0.7641 \cdot 2^{-14}$ | [JST1996] | As quoted in [Fra2002]. |
+| $51162598917 \cdot 2^{-50} = 0.744513802303 \cdot 2^{-14}$ | [Fra2002] | Blow-ups of the Cayley graph on $\mathbb{Z}\_2^{10}$ in which $x \sim y$ iff $\lvert x \triangle y \rvert \in \\{1,3,4,7,8,10\\}$, with red inside the blocks. |
+| $0.7445 \cdot 2^{-14}$ | [DFL2012] | Computational framework for such constructions. |
+| $0.7422548616 \cdot 2^{-14}$* | [SK2026] | Exact value $180244428715156181493112659521741405180580225001966676111887908798425648907356856409/3978585891278293137243057985174566720803649206378781739523711815145275976100267004264448 = 4.530364145469\ldots \times 10^{-5} = 0.742254861593625\ldots \cdot 2^{-14}$. A step graphon on the $1024$ blocks of [Fra2002] in which the red density between blocks $x, y$ depends only on $\lvert x \triangle y \rvert$, with values $n\_w / 2^{20}$, $(n\_0, \ldots, n\_{10}) = (1048576, 461327, 0, 1048576, 1048576, 13579, 0, 1048576, 1048576, 0, 799568)$, found by L-BFGS-B from Franek's point. The density is a sum over the $\binom{41}{10}$ multisets of column types of five vectors in $\mathbb{Z}\_2^{10}$. Two separately written exact evaluators (integer numerator modulo $61$-bit primes, combined by CRT) give the same fraction and reproduce [Fra2002] exactly. Data and checkers at commit `98b6ee3` of [SK2026]. Asterisked: self-hosted and not independently replayed. |
+
+## Known lower bounds
+
+| Bound | Reference | Comments |
+| ----- | --------- | -------- |
+| $1/\binom{252}{6} \approx 3.0 \times 10^{-12}$ | [ES1935] | Averaging: every 2-colouring of $K\_{252}$ contains a monochromatic $K\_6$, since $R(6,6) \le \binom{10}{5} = 252$. Better Ramsey-number upper bounds improve this slightly. |
+| $0.000021083 = 0.3454 \cdot 2^{-14}$* | [Pin2026] | Exact eight-vertex sum-of-squares certificate in the flag algebra of $2$-coloured graphs, with no Ramsey-number input. Two exact verifiers. |
+
+## Additional comments
+
+- No dedicated lower bound for $c\_6$ appears in the literature. Flag algebra computations of the size used for $c\_4$ and $c\_5$ are out of reach at $t = 6$. General lower bounds of the form $c\_t \ge C^{-(1+o(1))t^2}$ are due to [Con2012].
+- [DFL2012] also give $c\_7 \le 0.6869 \cdot 2^{-20}$ and $c\_8 \le 0.7002 \cdot 2^{-27}$.
+
+## References
+
